<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lambert I, Count of Louvain</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 950–1015</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Lambert the Bearded</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lambert I (c. 950–1015), called the Bearded, was the first Count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leuven">Louvain</a>, a younger son of the Reginarid count Reginar III of Hainaut. From around 1003 he built up lands around Leuven and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brussels">Brussels</a>, laying the foundations of the later Duchy of Brabant. He was killed at the Battle of Florennes in 1015 fighting Duke Godfrey II of Lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorraine">Lorraine</a>.</p></div>
